+> STOP. Captain's notes: non-binding. Captain writes, Captain trims. Anyone else: close this file now.
+
+# Captain Notes
+
+Binding behaviour lives in `.feature` specs and referenced `assets/**`. History lives in git. These notes carry only what the next cycle needs.
+
+## Current voyage: TodoMVC build
+
+**Status:** Specs authored, watchbill written. Awaiting QM dispatch.
+
+**Base commit:** `5646c7d todomvc: empty project with spec + template assets`
+
+**Feature files written (6):**
+- `features/todo-add.feature` -- new todo entry (6 scenarios)
+- `features/todo-display.feature` -- counter, visibility, clear completed (9 scenarios)
+- `features/todo-complete.feature` -- individual and toggle-all completion (6 scenarios)
+- `features/todo-edit.feature` -- editing, save, discard, empty destroy (6 scenarios)
+- `features/todo-routing.feature` -- hash routes, filtering, link highlighting (7 scenarios)
+- `features/todo-persistence.feature` -- localStorage survival across reload (1 scenario)
+
+**Total:** 35 product-lane scenarios across 6 features.
+
+**Watchbill:** 6 watches, ordered add -> display -> complete -> edit -> routing -> persistence. The build order reflects dependency: display depends on add; complete depends on both; edit is independent of complete; routing depends on complete for filtered-state assertions; persistence covers the full state.
+
+**Key decisions:**
+- Routing scenarios use `#/` prefix per the spec. The template links use `#/`, `#/active`, `#/completed`.
+- Editing step definitions will need DOM manipulation for double-click and blur events via happy-dom.
+- The spec's `autofocus` attribute on the new-todo input is checked in the "focused on page load" scenario.
+- "Mark all as complete" checkbox state is tracked: checked when all completed, unchecked when not all completed, cleared after clear-completed.
+
+**No open exclusions from assets.** The `assets/app-spec.md` is fully consumed by the specs above.
+
+**Next role:** QM. Context MUST clear before QM dispatch (Captain-to-QM bulkhead).
