@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+Feature: Add todo
+  As a user
+  I want to add new todos by typing a title and pressing Enter
+  So that I can capture tasks I need to do
+
+  Rule: New todo entry
+
+    Scenario: New todo input is focused on page load
+      Given the app is loaded
+      Then the new todo input has focus
+
+    Scenario: Creating a todo by pressing Enter
+      Given the app is loaded
+      When the user types "Buy milk" in the new todo input
+      And the user presses Enter
+      Then a todo "Buy milk" exists in the todo list
+      And the new todo input is empty
+
+    Scenario: Empty input does not create a todo
+      Given the app is loaded
+      When the user types "" in the new todo input
+      And the user presses Enter
+      Then the todo list is empty
+
+    Scenario: Whitespace-only input does not create a todo
+      Given the app is loaded
+      When the user types "   " in the new todo input
+      And the user presses Enter
+      Then the todo list is empty
+
+    Scenario: Input is trimmed before creating a todo
+      Given the app is loaded
+      When the user types "  Buy milk  " in the new todo input
+      And the user presses Enter
+      Then a todo "Buy milk" exists in the todo list
+
+    Scenario: Multiple todos can be added
+      Given the app is loaded
+      When the user types "Buy milk" in the new todo input
+      And the user presses Enter
+      And the user types "Walk the dog" in the new todo input
+      And the user presses Enter
+      Then the todo list contains 2 items
diff --git a/features/todo-complete.feature b/features/todo-complete.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0dc4c02
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-complete.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+Feature: Complete todo
+  As a user
+  I want to mark individual todos as complete and toggle all at once
+  So that I can track progress on my tasks
+
+  Rule: Individual completion
+
+    Scenario: Clicking the checkbox marks a todo as completed
+      Given the app is loaded
+      When the user adds a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user completes the todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+
+    Scenario: Counter excludes completed todos
+      Given the app is loaded
+      When the user adds a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user adds a todo "Walk the dog"
+      And the user completes the todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the counter displays "1 item left"
+
+  Rule: Mark all as complete
+
+    Scenario: Toggle all marks every todo as completed
+      Given the app is loaded
+      When the user adds a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user adds a todo "Walk the dog"
+      And the user clicks the toggle all checkbox
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+      And the todo "Walk the dog" is completed
+      And the toggle all checkbox is checked
+      And the counter displays "0 items left"
+
+    Scenario: Toggle all unchecks when a todo is unchecked
+      Given the app is loaded
+      When the user adds a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user adds a todo "Walk the dog"
+      And the user clicks the toggle all checkbox
+      And the user uncompletes the todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the toggle all checkbox is not checked
+
+    Scenario: Toggle all checks when all todos are completed
+      Given the app is loaded
+      When the user adds a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user adds a todo "Walk the dog"
+      And the user completes the todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user completes the todo "Walk the dog"
+      Then the toggle all checkbox is checked
+
+    Scenario: Toggle all clears completed state after clear completed
+      Given the app is loaded
+      When the user adds a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user adds a todo "Walk the dog"
+      And the user clicks the toggle all checkbox
+      And the user clicks the clear completed button
+      Then the toggle all checkbox is not checked
diff --git a/features/todo-display.feature b/features/todo-display.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5102a78
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-display.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,64 @@
+Feature: Todo display
+  As a user
+  I want to see the correct item count and section visibility
+  So that I understand the current state of my todos
+
+  Rule: Active counter
+
+    Scenario: Counter shows zero items when list is empty
+      Given the app is loaded
+      Then the counter displays "0 items left"
+
+    Scenario: Counter shows singular form for one active item
+      Given the app is loaded
+      When the user adds a todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the counter displays "1 item left"
+
+    Scenario: Counter shows plural form for multiple active items
+      Given the app is loaded
+      When the user adds a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user adds a todo "Walk the dog"
+      Then the counter displays "2 items left"
+
+    Scenario: Counter only counts active items
+      Given the app is loaded
+      When the user adds a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user adds a todo "Walk the dog"
+      And the user completes the todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the counter displays "1 item left"
+
+  Rule: Section visibility
+
+    Scenario: Main and footer are hidden when there are no todos
+      Given the app is loaded
+      Then the main section is hidden
+      And the footer is hidden
+
+    Scenario: Main and footer appear when a todo is added
+      Given the app is loaded
+      When the user adds a todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the main section is visible
+      And the footer is visible
+
+  Rule: Clear completed button
+
+    Scenario: Clear completed button is hidden when no completed todos exist
+      Given the app is loaded
+      When the user adds a todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the clear completed button is hidden
+
+    Scenario: Clear completed button is visible when completed todos exist
+      Given the app is loaded
+      When the user adds a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user completes the todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the clear completed button is visible
+
+    Scenario: Clear completed button removes completed todos
+      Given the app is loaded
+      When the user adds a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user adds a todo "Walk the dog"
+      And the user completes the todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user clicks the clear completed button
+      Then a todo "Walk the dog" exists in the todo list
+      And a todo "Buy milk" does not exist
+      And the counter displays "1 item left"
diff --git a/features/todo-edit.feature b/features/todo-edit.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..625a522
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-edit.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,61 @@
+Feature: Edit todo
+  As a user
+  I want to double-click a todo to edit its title
+  So that I can correct or update tasks after creation
+
+  Rule: Editing mode activation
+
+    Scenario: Double-clicking a todo activates editing mode
+      Given the app is loaded
+      When the user adds a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user double-clicks the todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+
+  Rule: Saving edits
+
+    Scenario: Pressing Enter saves the edit
+      Given the app is loaded
+      When the user adds a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user double-clicks the todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user types "Buy oat milk" in the edit input
+      And the user presses Enter
+      Then a todo "Buy oat milk" exists in the todo list
+      And a todo "Buy milk" does not exist
+
+    Scenario: Blurring saves the edit
+      Given the app is loaded
+      When the user adds a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user double-clicks the todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user types "Buy oat milk" in the edit input
+      And the edit input loses focus
+      Then a todo "Buy oat milk" exists in the todo list
+      And a todo "Buy milk" does not exist
+
+  Rule: Discarding edits
+
+    Scenario: Pressing Escape discards the edit
+      Given the app is loaded
+      When the user adds a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user double-clicks the todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user types "Buy oat milk" in the edit input
+      And the user presses Escape
+      Then a todo "Buy milk" exists in the todo list
+      And a todo "Buy oat milk" does not exist
+
+  Rule: Empty title destroys the todo
+
+    Scenario: Saving an empty edit removes the todo
+      Given the app is loaded
+      When the user adds a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user double-clicks the todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user types "" in the edit input
+      And the user presses Enter
+      Then a todo "Buy milk" does not exist
+
+    Scenario: Saving a whitespace-only edit removes the todo
+      Given the app is loaded
+      When the user adds a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user double-clicks the todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user types "   " in the edit input
+      And the user presses Enter
+      Then a todo "Buy milk" does not exist
diff --git a/features/todo-persistence.feature b/features/todo-persistence.feature
new file mode 100644
